                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Loved this game when I was younger and wanted to try it again to see how I would feel about it now and honestly, its not that bad. It has a lot of lows but it has some peaks that don't reach super high, but are high enough to be appreciated.\r\nGame didn't really drag on enough to be boring. Modern sonic levels were okay they weren't boring and had a few cool gimmicks or alternate paths but compared to other sonic games they didn't really offer much. They also just didn't control very well. The avatar as a whole was pretty solid aside from the uncomfortable platforming. The wispons were cool and they found some ways to make the stages somewhat engaging. Soundtrack is solid as always, not as consistent but has some great songs (along with some pretty bad ones). Story is questionable and classic sonic Isn't great. Definitely the lowlight of the game but the stages didn't drag on enough for me to get sick of them. Overall some cool ideas but poor execution.\r\nI could see a new player having some fun with this but not someone coming from generations or unleashed. Its not a bad game at all. Its just alright. Does it live up to the quality of generations or unleashed? No. Is it worth $40? No. Is it the worst game in the series? \r\nNo.\r\n6.5/10",
